# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# The v1 fault catalogue (platform plan D-PLq). JSON; whole-line "#"
# comments are allowed, as in QEMU's QAPI files.
#
# "changes": truth for a physical failure (the platform stops sending,
# a link carries nothing), presented for a wrong reading (the HK ADC
# forcings): the attenuator plan's amendment to D-PLo.
#
# The attenuator track's A-3 set is in the list below: one qom
# property per id on /machine/stixctrl/attenuator (their plan's fault
# catalogue, D-Ag; expected_detection stays empty until a live PFM run
# confirms the outcomes). The A-later rows stay reserved:
#   attenuator.move.slow, attenuator.mechanism.partial,
#   attenuator.motor1.flag_lost, attenuator.motor2.flag_lost,
#   attenuator.controller.fail_flag, attenuator.current.scale.
#
# Reserved for the flash-damage track (docs/stix-port/
# 2026-11-12-flash-damage-plan.md, D-X5), comment-only until the
# platform track adopts the IDs: every real row is validated into an
# injectable fault, so a reservation can only live here, as with the
# attenuator IDs above.
#   flash.block.erase_fail, flash.page.program_fail, flash.cell.stuck
#     -- device faults: class memory, changes truth, persistence
#     until_cleared, reversible; params block|page (+bit, value) in the
#     FSW-linear index space; action qom with property damage-add and
#     clear damage-remove on /machine/stixflash (needs the platform's
#     qom-path pattern to reach that device first).
#   flash.block.bad_factory, flash.file.corrupt, flash.file.wrong_address
#     -- offline setup rows, no action: expressed as pre-boot scenario
#     steps (the planned hooks.* verb flash.damage running
#     scripts/stix/flash-damage.py), never injectable faults (D-X5).
